  "slug": "tumor-cell-0358",
  "summary": "23 published reports, no preprints, code, or industry items; focus on tumor-cell states, stroma, and macrophage niches via scRNA-seq and spatial omics.",
  "synthesis": "The window contains 23 published items and no preprint, code, or industry entries. Single-cell and spatial transcriptomics anchor much of the activity. In PDAC, scRNA-seq with spatial profiling identifies invasive-frontier myCAFs and a tumor-stroma community, and SPP1-CD44 endothelial-macrophage crosstalk upregulates S100A6. In lung adenocarcinoma, SPP1+ macrophage-derived WNT5A is linked to MMP11+ myCAF matrix remodeling and PD-1 blockade resistance. Other studies map melanoma stemness niches, derive a six-gene cholangiocarcinoma prognostic signature, and nominate CTHRC1+ fibroblasts as stroma biomarkers in colorectal cancer. Reviews extend the framing to cell plasticity, UPR-based proteostatic states, and epigenetic memory. The rise ratio reflects published volume only; these items do not establish a cause for it.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-12"
}
